QNX support: io-sock is the FreeBSD network stack, so QNX takes scapy's FreeBSD/BPF path (PF_ROUTE, /dev/bpf). Differences handled here: /dev/bpf is a cloning device (no /dev/bpfN); QNX's _IO() has no direction bits (BIOCPROMISC, BIOCFLUSH); a new BPF descriptor sees no packet until BIOCSETF was issued twice; ctypes.util.find_library() finds nothing, so libpcap is loaded by soname.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

